{"event": "policy_compiled", "run_id": "618f612799574b0786cd6b5c45ee6975", "pid": 14576, "time": "2026-10-10T11:01:14-0700", "elapsed_s": 176.776, "artifact": "out/det-ab-1.policy.json", "bands": 2, "identity_fields": ["date_of_birth", "phone_last4"], "special_cases": ["already_paid", "dispute", "hardship", "restructuring", "human", "scam", "robot", "refuse_to_talk", "cannot_answer", "change_recorded_promise"], "unresolved": [{"topic": "hardship_multi_product", "text": "Brief B lists hardship as an add_note reason but does not say whether a declined hardship transfer ends the call or continues with the other products (Brief B rule 9 names only dispute and already paid); kept Brief A behaviour (close as no_promise / hardship after noting unpromised products).", "doc": "sources/001-brief-b.md"}, {"topic": "missing_date_parts", "text": "Neither brief says how to read a promise or callback date given without a month or year (e.g. 'the 15th'); left as unresolved.", "doc": "sources/000-brief-a.md"}, {"topic": "no_extra_terms", "text": "Rule 33 (never offer a discount, a waiver, an instalment plan or any term not in the brief) has no structural IR field; it must be carried by the prompt text.", "doc": "sources/000-brief-a.md"}], "audit_fixed": ["phrases.opening: removed the invented 'Hello,'. Rule 1 only gives the content, so the sentence now says just that (opening_verbatim stays false).", "phrases.all_today_question: reworded to follow Brief B rule 4 ('whether the customer can pay all of them today') more closely.", "special_cases[hardship].source: added the rule 32 sentence that supports takes_promise=true ('If the customer still names a date or an amount themselves, record the promise').", "identity.source: added the rule 15 decline text that supports declined_outcome and asking_purpose_counts_as_decline.", "third_party.source: added rule 10 (a relative may not answer questions or be told anything).", "calendar.source: added rule 22 (next <weekday>) that supports next_weekday_means_following_week.", "unresolved: added missing_date_parts (neither brief settles it) and no_extra_terms (rule 33 has no IR field)."], "audit_unresolved": ["Hardship with several products: Brief B does not say whether a declined support transfer ends the call or the call continues with the other products. Brief A behaviour kept (ends_call=true).", "How to read a date given without a month or year is not specified.", "Rule 33 (no discounts, waivers, instalment plans or other terms) has no structural field and must go in the prompt text."]}
